# BNOW.NET — environment-variable EXAMPLES (documentation only).
#
# Every line is commented on purpose: this file must never carry an active
# assignment or a secret. Copy the lines you need into your own .env.local
# (gitignored) or the Vercel environment. The authoritative credentials table
# lives in AGENTS.md; spend-cap semantics are standing ruling 4.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloud-model routing (src/lib/llm/model-config.ts) — resolved at CALL time.
# Precedence per analysis workload: <WORKLOAD>_MODEL → OPENAI_MODEL → gpt-4o-mini.
# Blank/whitespace values are treated as absent. Dispatch FAILS CLOSED unless
# the resolved model has BOTH an exact price in src/lib/llm/pricing.ts
# PRICES_PER_MTOK and a quality-registry approval for the exact (workload,
# model, effort) in src/lib/llm/analysis-registry.ts — pricing alone is not
# quality approval. Reasoning efforts accept minimal|low|medium|high, apply
# only to reasoning models (gpt-5 family / o-series), and FAIL CLOSED when
# invalid or set on a non-reasoning model.
#
# MAP IS ADDITIONALLY HARD-LOCKED to its baseline (gpt-4o-mini, no effort):
# changing MAP_MODEL or MAP_REASONING_EFFORT changes mapExtractorVersion() but
# does NOT remap historical documents by itself (the hourly worker selects
# processed=false docs only), so every consumer of current-version claims
# would starve until the corpus is explicitly remapped. The version-aware
# remap operator exists (scripts/map-remap.ts — dry-run-first, resumable,
# lease-safe; OPEN-TASKS #33), but the lock stays: any non-baseline map
# configuration fails closed with "MAP ACTIVATION BLOCKED" — no env override
# exists; explicit operator activation authorization (with a costed remap of
# the corpus) relaxes it. REDUCE_MODEL changes are independent and never trip it.
# Inspect the resolved matrix without any provider call:
#   npx tsx scripts/model-routing-inspect.ts
#
# NONE of these are set anywhere today (2026-08-17). Activating any of them is
# gated on: verified pricing in pricing.ts, request-compatibility checks, a
# representative paid evaluation, spend-cap review, and operator authorization
# (docs/reviews/CLOUD-MODEL-ROUTING-SEAMS-2026-08-17.md § activation checklist).
#
# OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # global fallback for every analysis workload
# MAP_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini                 # map stage (per-doc claim extraction)
# MAP_REASONING_EFFORT=low              # reasoning models only
# REDUCE_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # mapreduce digest synthesis votes
# REDUCE_REASONING_EFFORT=medium        # reasoning models only
# DIGEST_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini              # legacy digest extraction
# DIGEST_REASONING_EFFORT=low           # reasoning models only
# VALIDATION_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini          # ISW scoreboard LLM matcher
# VALIDATION_REASONING_EFFORT=low       # reasoning models only
# ENTITY_AUDIT_MODEL=gpt-4o-mini        # propose-only entity audit
# ENTITY_AUDIT_REASONING_EFFORT=low     # reasoning models only
#
# Per-workload PROVIDER (2026-09 provider dimension). Default openai; the value
# is validated against a per-workload allowlist BEFORE any other check, and a
# provider other than openai requires an explicit <WORKLOAD>_MODEL (OPENAI_MODEL
# and the gpt-4o-mini default apply to provider openai only). Every allowlist is
# {openai} today, so these envs are a refusal surface, not a routing surface:
# widening one is a reviewed PR plus a decision-log entry, and even then the
# model must be priced FOR THAT PROVIDER in pricing.ts and approved for the
# exact (workload, provider, model, effort) in analysis-registry.ts. Map accepts
# openai only. ANALYSIS_PROVIDER is NOT a routing switch (stub = the offline
# extractor; anthropic = refused — see OPEN-TASKS #83). Every value below is
# ABSENT in every environment today.
# MAP_PROVIDER=openai
# REDUCE_PROVIDER=openai
# DIGEST_PROVIDER=openai
# VALIDATION_PROVIDER=openai
# ENTITY_AUDIT_PROVIDER=openai
#
# Ask pipeline models are NOT routed by model-config (scorecard-gated —
# src/lib/ask/registry.ts):
# ASK_ANSWER_MODEL=gpt-5
# ASK_RERANK_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
#
# The embedding model is not routed by model-config either, but it IS priced:
# a model with no row in EMBED_PRICES_PER_MTOK (src/lib/llm/pricing.ts) is
# refused before any reservation and before the SDK client is built, so Ask
# degrades to lexical-only retrieval and the backfill script exits non-zero.
# Swapping the model means adding an operator-verified price row first — and
# note that existing claim_embeddings rows are keyed by model, so a swap also
# needs a backfill before vector retrieval finds anything.
# ASK_EMBED_MODEL=text-embedding-3-small

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vercel log-drain receiver (src/app/api/logs/drain/route.ts, table runtime_logs;
# OPEN-TASKS #93, docs/designs/LOG-DRAIN.md). Gives soak windows an independent
# in-window narrative instead of `cron_runs` self-reports plus an expired
# `vercel logs` tail.
#
# LOG_DRAIN_SECRET is the drain's signature secret: Vercel sends the hex
# HMAC-SHA1 of the raw body in `x-vercel-signature`, and the value here must
# equal the one in the drain's dashboard configuration. It FAILS CLOSED — while
# it is unset or blank the route answers 503, reads no body and writes nothing,
# so an unconfigured receiver can never accept unauthenticated data. It is not a
# spend cap, but it carries ruling 4's ORDERING: set it in Production BEFORE the
# receiver deploys, or every delivery 503s until it appears (which trips
# Vercel's errored-drain notification and reads like an incident).
#
# Register the drain only AFTER that deploy: Vercel dashboard -> Team Settings
# -> Drains -> Add Drain -> Logs -> project bnow-net -> sources `lambda`,
# environment `production`, sampling rule 1 = path prefix /api/logs/drain at 0%
# and rule 2 = blank prefix at 100% (kills the self-ingestion loop at source),
# destination Custom endpoint https://bnow.net/api/logs/drain, format NDJSON.
# Full runbook: docs/designs/LOG-DRAIN.md §8.
#
# LOG_DRAIN_SECRET=<32+ random bytes, hex or base64; same value as the drain's>
#
# The rest are bounded in-code defaults — leaving them unset does NOT disable
# anything. Retention deliberately does NOT fail closed on a bad value (failing
# closed on retention would mean "keep forever"): an invalid, blank or <=0 value
# falls back to 14 days.
# LOG_DRAIN_RETENTION_DAYS=14        # rows are deleted once received_at is older
# LOG_DRAIN_MAX_ROWS=1000            # rows stored per delivery; the rest are dropped, never blocked
# LOG_DRAIN_MAX_BODY_BYTES=4000000   # oversized body -> 200 with stored 0 (never a retryable status)
# LOG_DRAIN_SWEEP_LIMIT=5000         # rows deleted per hourly retention pass

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Map-stage concurrency lease (src/lib/analysis/map-lease.ts, provider_state
# key 'map_lease'): serializes the hourly cron, the backfill driver, and the
# remap operator. TTL seconds; clamped to [30, 600] so it can neither thrash
# nor outlive the map route's 800s maxDuration. Default 120.
# MAP_LEASE_TTL_SEC=120

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Analysis-eval control plane (src/lib/evals, scripts/analysis-eval.ts).
# Live candidate evaluation is OPERATOR-GATED and has never run. Two caps fail
# CLOSED — unset means live dispatch is refused everywhere: EVAL_USD_CAP_DAILY
# (deliberately no out-of-production default) and the shared all-time backstop
# LLM_SPRINT_USD_CAP (the every-OpenAI-path total cap, ruling 4; also checked
# by the live preflight). EVAL_DAILY_REQUEST_CAP / EVAL_RUN_REQUEST_CAP are
# bounded in-code defaults (300/200) — leaving them unset does NOT block a
# run, it applies the defaults. EVAL_DATABASE_URL must point at a disposable
# eval branch and be acknowledged with --db-ack <host>; DATABASE_URL is never
# read by live mode. Set caps BEFORE any live run (ruling 4 ordering).
# LLM_SPRINT_USD_CAP=10
# EVAL_USD_CAP_DAILY=2
# EVAL_DAILY_REQUEST_CAP=300
# EVAL_RUN_REQUEST_CAP=200
# EVAL_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...disposable-eval-branch...
